  "assumptions": [
    "Users are identified by UUID primary keys for better scalability and security",
    "Email verification is required before full platform access",
    "Study notes are stored in AWS S3 with URLs saved in the database",
    "Rating system uses integer values from 1 to 5",
    "Average rating is stored as varchar to allow for decimal precision display",
    "Group creators automatically become group admins",
    "Users can subscribe to subjects to receive notifications about new notes",
    "Notifications support polymorphic references to different entity types",
    "Group messages are stored separately to support group discussions",
    "All timestamps use CURRENT_TIMESTAMP for automatic tracking",
    "Soft delete is not implemented; is_active flags are used where needed",
    "File metadata (size, type, name) is stored for better file management",
    "Download count is tracked for analytics and popularity metrics",
    "Users can only rate notes once (enforced by unique constraint on user_id and note_id combination)",
    "Group membership is tracked through junction table to support many-to-many relationship"
  ]
}